  "text": "Oncology Archives – University of Pennsylvania, School of Veterinary Medicine\nSkip to main content\nSkip to veterinary school Navigation\nSkip to veterinary hospital Navigation\nGo to site search\nUniversity of Pennsylvania, School of Veterinary Medicine logo\n- - -\nSchool of Veterinary Medicine\nBack\nPrograms\nBack\nVMD Curriculum\nLearn more\nPrograms\nVMD Degree\nThe Veterinariae Medicinae Doctoris (VMD) degree is designed to prepare students for careers in veterinary practice, research, and public health.\nDual Degree Programs\nVMD | PhD\nVMD | MSW\nVMD | MPH\nVMD | ML\nVMD | MBA\nVMD | MES\nVMD | MSTR\nVMD Admissions\nHow to Apply\nTimeline\nTuition and Aid\nContact Admissions\nOne Health\nOther Programs\nOnline Graduate Programs in Animal Welfare & Behavior\nCertificates & Continuing Education\nStudent Life\nBack\nStudent Life\nLearn More\nLife Outside of Class\nLearn More\nStudent Life\nLife Outside of Class\nTraining Opportunities\nStudent Stories\nCareer Counseling\nAlumni\nDepartments & Faculty\nBack\nAcademic Departments\nLearn More\nAcademic Departments\nBiomedical Sciences\nClinical Sciences & Advanced Medicine\nClinical Studies – New Bolton Center\nPathobiology\nFaculty Directory\nResearch\nBack\nResearch at Penn Vet\nLearn More\nResearch\nCenters\nCenter for Animal Transgenesis & Germ Cell Research\nCenter for Stewardship Agriculture and Food Security\nSwine Teaching and Research Center\nPenn Vet Cancer Center\nPenn Vet Working Dog Center\nInstitute\nInstitute for Infectious & Zoonotic Diseases\nResearch Programs\nComparative Immunotherapy Program\nDivision of  Experimental Retinal Therapies\nShelter Medicine and Community Engagement Program\nThe Swine Group\nWildlife Futures Program\nResearch Laboratories\nCore Labs\nAbout\nBack\nNews\nLearn More\nOffice of the Dean\nLearn More\nAbout\nNews\nOffice of the Dean\nEvents\nOne Health\nGiving\nCommunity and Engagement\nBellwether Magazine\nAccreditation\nContact\nVeterinary Hospitals\nBack\nVeterinary Hospitals\nLearn More\nRyan Hospital\nCare for cats, dogs & other companion animals\nBy Appointment\n215-746-8387\nFor Emergencies\n215-746-8911\nFind Us\n3900 Spruce Street Philadelphia, PA 19104\nNew Bolton Center Hospital\nCare for horses & livestock/farm animals\nFor Appointments & Emergencies\n610-444-5800\nFind Us\n382 West Street Road Kennett Square, PA 19348\nApply\nAlumni\nGive\nContact Penn Vet\nApply\nAlumni\nGive\nContact Penn Vet\nSearch.....\nOncology\nFLASH-Based Radioimmunotherapy in Canine Glioma\nThe purpose of this study is to evaluate the feasibility, safety, and efficacy of FLASH proton radiation therapy (FLASH-RT), administered either alone or in combination with Gilvetmab, as a treatment…\nSeptember 29, 2026\nEvaluation of Proton FLASH-RT in Naturally Occurring Canine Extremity Sarcoma\nProton FLASH radiation therapy (FLASH-RT) is an investigational approach using ultra-high dose “RATE” radiation therapy. This means that the dose(s) of radiation is delivered in a fraction of a second.…\nMay 13, 2025\nCell Therapy for Metastatic Osteosarcoma\nIn this study we will investigate the therapeutic potential of a type of white blood cell known as invariant natural killer T (iNKT) cells that are made from the blood…\nJanuary 2, 2025\nPSMA Ligand Based Theranostic to Treat Canine Prostatic Cancer\nThe purpose of this study is to assess a new targeted investigational agent called PSMA-MMAE-Pc413 combined with a laser in local and metastatic disease in dogs diagnosed with prostate cancer.\nDecember 10, 2024\nPalliative-intent radiation therapy and frunevetmab (Solensia) for feline bone-invasive oral squamous cell carcinoma: A pilot study.\nThis study will be the first to assess whether Solensia, in combination with meloxicam and palliative-intent radiation therapy, provides superior pain relief compared to meloxicam and radiation therapy alone. Meloxicam,…\nApril 12, 2024\nNear-infrared imaging of canine lung tumors during surgery\nThe aim of this study is to improve detection of surgical margins and metastatic lymph nodes at the time of surgery to remove the tumor. This is vital in both…\nOctober 14, 2020\nSort By\nSpecies\nDogs (5)\nCats (1)\nTrial Status\nRecruiting (5)\nUniversity of Pennsylvania, School of Veterinary Medicine logo\nApply\nContact Penn Vet\nGive\nFind us\nSchool of Veterinary Medicine\n3800 Spruce Street,\nPhiladelphia, PA 19104\nSee Our Veterinary Hospitals\nFollow Us\nSECTIONS\nAbout\nAccreditation\nCareers at Penn Vet\nEmergency Info\nFaculty Directory\nInside.PennVet Portal\nMedia and Press Inquiries\nPenn Vet Library\nPenn Vet News\nPrograms\nResearch\nStudent Life\nReport Accessibility Issues\nUniversity of Pennsylvania\nPrivacy Policy\n© 2026 University of Pennsylvania, School of Veterinary Medicine",
